{%- comment -%}
  ─── THE WISHLIST PANEL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  A SHELL, NOT A LIST. Loved products live in `localStorage` ("mc-loved" /
  "mc-loved-meta", written by the heart button on a card — see
  marathon-storefront.js) and can be loved from any product on any page, so
  there is no set of product IDs known at RENDER time to loop over here. This
  snippet only prints the empty dialog frame, once, in `theme.liquid`, global
  like the panel it borrows its look from (`.mc-panel` in marathon-card.liquid).
  marathon-storefront.js fills `[data-mc-wishlist-list]` with real rows —
  photo, price, remove, add-to-cart or a link to the product page — every time
  the panel opens, so a card loved or unloved on a DIFFERENT page since the
  last open is never shown stale.

  SUPERSEDED AS THE PRIMARY ENTRY POINT (owner order 2026-08-27): the header
  heart in sections/header.liquid now links straight to a real page
  (`sections/marathon-loved.liquid` via `templates/page.loved.json`) instead
  of opening this overlay — a shopper can navigate to it, bookmark it, or
  reload on it, none of which a JS-only panel supports. This snippet is left
  in place, still rendered globally by theme.liquid, as inert markup: nothing
  currently opens it, but nothing breaks if some other entry point ever does
  again, since marathon-storefront.js's `renderAllWishlists()` populates every
  `[data-mc-wishlist-list]` on the page, this one included.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="mc-panel mc-wishlist" hidden data-mc-wishlist-panel role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Loved products">
  <div class="mc-panel__sheet mc-wishlist__sheet" data-mc-sheet>
    <button type="button" class="mc-panel__close" data-mc-wishlist-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <p class="mc-head__title mc-wishlist__title">Loved</p>

    {%- comment -%}
      EMPTY STATE lives in the markup from the start, `hidden` by default, and
      is un-hidden by script only when the loved list is actually empty — so
      there is never a blank panel while JavaScript decides what to show.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="mc-wishlist__empty" data-mc-wishlist-empty hidden>
      Nothing loved yet. Tap the heart on a photograph to keep it here.
    </p>

    <div class="mc-wishlist__list" data-mc-wishlist-list></div>
  </div>
</div>
